gned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,-6)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{2-(-6)}{4-9}(x-9) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{8}{-5}(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =-\\frac{8}{5}(x-9) \\\\ 5y+30 & =-8x+72 \\\\ 8x+5y & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n8x+5y=42\n$$" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280950 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280951 13194139534181 true] [17592186280950 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534181 true] [17592186280950 1041 "field-1" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280950 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280951 13194139534181 true] [17592186280950 1110 #uuid "cdbd96d5-67fa-52eb-9b72-b1a6da45dacd" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280951 1034 "8x+5y" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534181 true] [17592186280951 1111 #uuid "9c6784ba-0bcf-5132-b031-9ca99c91e25b" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280952 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280953 13194139534181 true] [17592186280952 1089 "q-281586" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280952 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534181 true] [17592186280952 1100 "Consider the line $-4x+y+1=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=6.$" 13194139534181 true] [17592186280952 1113 #uuid "534b0fc4-23b